# =============================================================================
# JR One - Vercel upload exclusions
# =============================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-08-08):
# `vercel --prod` uploads the working DIRECTORY, not the git tree. Vercel does
# NOT read .gitignore. Proof: `.claude-flow/` is gitignored at .gitignore line
# 42 and is untracked by git (`git ls-files .claude-flow` returns nothing), yet
# https://www.jronegutters.com/.claude-flow/data/pending-insights.jsonl served
# HTTP 200 with 304 bytes of local agent edit-telemetry. A gitignored file was
# public on the customer-facing site.
#
# So every "keep it out of the repo" rule in .gitignore has to be restated here
# or it does not apply to production.
#
# BUT DO NOT BLINDLY MIRROR .gitignore. It carries `public/images/*.png`
# (.gitignore:43), which excludes SERVED site assets. Mirroring that line would
# strip images off the live site. .gitignore answers "what should not be
# committed"; this file answers "what should not be published". They overlap,
# they are not the same question.
#
# ── TWO RULES FOR EDITING THIS FILE ──
# 1. ANCHOR EVERY DIRECTORY WITH A LEADING SLASH. Gitignore syntax matches a
#    bare `projects/` at ANY depth, which would have excluded `app/projects/`
#    and 404'd a live route. Every directory below is anchored to the repo root
#    on purpose. Verified with:
#      find app components lib content public -type d -name projects
#      -> app/projects   (a real route, must ship)
# 2. Excluding something the build needs breaks the live site. Anything the
#    build or runtime touches is listed under KEEP and must never be added.
#
# KEEP (verified required, do NOT exclude):
#   app/ components/ lib/ content/ public/
#   scripts/        - package.json runs `postbuild`: node scripts/check-sitemap.mjs
#   lib/city-service-es.js - read by check-sitemap.mjs:49 (ES_SOURCE)
#   content/blog, content/blog-es - read by lib/blog.js:7-8 via process.cwd()
#   next.config.js middleware.js jsconfig.json package.json package-lock.json
#   .browserslistrc
# =============================================================================

# ── Secrets. Vercel injects production env from its own dashboard, never from
#    an uploaded file, so shipping these buys nothing and risks everything.
#    .env.local is mode 600 locally and was being uploaded on every deploy.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── AI / agent tooling. `.claude-flow/data/pending-insights.jsonl` is the file
#    that was actually live at HTTP 200. The rest never should have been sent.
/.claude-flow/
/.claude/
/.cursor/
/.roo/
/.windsurf/
/.aider.conf.yml
.aider.tags.cache.v3/

# ── Build caches and artifacts. Vercel runs a clean install and a fresh build,
#    so uploading these only risks serving a stale local artifact.
/.next/
/out/
/build/
/dist/
/coverage/
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Version control and deploy state
/.git/
/.gitignore
/.gitattributes
/.github/
/.vercel/

# ── Python tooling (scripts/generate_documents.py is a local-only build step,
#    invoked by `npm run build:documents`, NOT by `npm run build`)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/.pytest_cache/
/.venv/
/venv/

# ── OS metadata. `.DS_Store` is gitignored but was still being uploaded.
#    Unanchored on purpose: these appear at every depth.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Editor and IDE
/.vscode/
/.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Backups and scratch. An in-repo backup of a served file is itself an
#    exposure, so these must never reach the deployment.
*.bak
*.backup
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.old

# ── Logs (verified: zero *.log files under app/ components/ lib/ content/ public/)
*.log
/logs/

# ── Internal / non-public working material. None of this is imported by app/,
#    components/, lib/ or content/ - the only matches were source-citation
#    COMMENTS, not imports. audit/ alone is 242M of CompanyCam analysis
#    carrying customer photo URLs.
/audit/
/internal-documents/
/projects/
/tools/
/docs/
/tests/

# ── 32M write-only debug log. lib/companycam/photo-filter.js:58 is the ONLY
#    code that names it and it only APPENDS (:76); nothing in the repo reads it
#    back (the sole other mention, :57, is a comment showing a manual jq
#    command). It is already gitignored at .gitignore:49. The directory is
#    recreated on demand by the mkdirSync at photo-filter.js:67, so excluding it
#    cannot break the writer.
/data/

# ── Internal markdown that has no route and no reader on the public site
/decisions-log.md
/manual-steps.md
/TESTING_GUIDE.md
/TESTING_INDEX.md
/TEST_COVERAGE_ANALYSIS.md
